'''Danté Exum'''<ref>{{cite web|last=Kamenetzky|first=Brian|url=https://www.redbull.com/us-en/dante-exum-australian-basketball-player-2014-nba-draft|title=Meet Danté Exum: The NBA Draft's Man of Mystery|publisher=[[Red Bull]]|date=20 February 2017|accessdate=6 June 2024}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.nba.com/jazz/news/guard-or-wing-dante-exum-keeping-open-mind-about-his-role-utah-jazz-season|title=Guard or wing? Danté Exum keeping an 'open mind' about his role with the Utah Jazz this season|website=[[National Basketball Association|NBA.com]]|date=5 October 2019|accessdate=6 June 2024}}</ref> ({{IPAc-en|ˈ|d|ɑː|n|t|eɪ|_|ˈ|ɛ|k|s|ə|m}} {{respell|DAHN|tay|_|EK|səm}}; born 13 July 1995) is an Australian professional [[basketball]] player who last played for the [[Dallas Mavericks]] of the [[National Basketball Association]] (NBA). He chose to bypass college and was ultimately selected by the [[Utah Jazz]] with the fifth overall pick in the [[2014 NBA draft]].<ref>{{cite magazine|last=Mannix|first=Chris|url=https://www.si.com/nba/2013/09/26/nba-draft-big-board-2014-andrew-wiggins|title=2014 NBA Big Board: Wiggins leads deepest draft in years|magazine=Sports Illustrated|date=26 September 2013|access-date=2 December 2016}}</ref>

Exum has played for the [[Australia men's national basketball team|Australia national team]] and won a bronze medal at the [[2020 Summer Olympics|2020 Tokyo Olympics]].
